From: Latch headless test fixture
Subject: Allow ScreenCast with wl_shm when the compositor has no DMA-BUF

xdg-desktop-portal-wlr 0.7.1 checks for DMA-BUF before it negotiates the
consumer's buffer type. A pixman headless compositor only offers wl_shm.
Keep the SHM format requirement and exercise the existing SHM producer.

Explicitly trigger the PipeWire graph after queuing a frame. PipeWire
1.0.5's implicit queue trigger requires the driver to be assigned already.
A static headless desktop can otherwise lose its only initial frame.

diff --git a/src/screencast/screencast.c b/src/screencast/screencast.c
--- a/src/screencast/screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/screencast.c
@@ -201,9 +201,7 @@ static int start_screencast(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast) {
 	wl_display_dispatch(cast->ctx->state->wl_display);
 	wl_display_roundtrip(cast->ctx->state->wl_display);
 
-	if (cast->screencopy_frame_info[WL_SHM].format == DRM_FORMAT_INVALID ||
-			(cast->ctx->state->screencast_version >= 3 &&
-			 cast->screencopy_frame_info[DMABUF].format == DRM_FORMAT_INVALID)) {
+	if (cast->screencopy_frame_info[WL_SHM].format == DRM_FORMAT_INVALID) {
 		logprint(INFO, "wlroots: unable to receive a valid format from wlr_screencopy");
 		return -1;
 	}
diff --git a/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c b/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
--- a/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
@@ -521,6 +521,7 @@ void xdpw_pwr_enqueue_buffer(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast) {
 	logprint(TRACE, "********************");
 
 	pw_stream_queue_buffer(cast->stream, pw_buf);
+	pw_stream_trigger_process(cast->stream);
 
 done:
 	cast->current_frame.xdpw_buffer = NULL;
